## v1.2 — Actions & Integrations 🔧

Extend the `steps:` system beyond `db.insert` / `db.update`.

### New Route Actions
- [ ] `http.post` — fire webhooks to external services
  ```yaml
  steps:
    - action: http.post
      url: "https://hooks.slack.com/xxx"
      input: "$event.payload"
  ```
- [ ] `http.get` — fetch data from external APIs during route execution
- [ ] `log.write` — append to a structured log file / stdout
- [ ] `db.query` — read from SQLite and inject results into the pipeline
- [ ] `db.delete` — remove rows by condition
- [ ] `transform` — reshape payload between steps
  ```yaml
  steps:
    - action: transform
      map:
        user_email: "$event.payload.email"
        created_at: "$now"
  ```

### Event Chaining
- [ ] Route A emits state → automatically triggers Route B
  ```yaml
  routes:
    - on: USER_SIGNUP
      steps:
        - action: db.insert
          table: users
      emit: USER_CREATED

    - on: USER_CREATED      # ← triggered by the emit above
      steps:
        - action: http.post
          url: "https://api.sendgrid.com/v3/send"
  ```

### Built-in Variables
- [ ] `$now` — current ISO timestamp
- [ ] `$uuid` — auto-generated UUID
- [ ] `$event.name` — the event that triggered this route
- [ ] `$env.SECRET_KEY` — environment variable access

---

## v1.3 — Conditional Logic & Middleware 🧠

Make routes smart with branching and guards.

### Conditional Routes
- [ ] `if:` conditions on routes
  ```yaml
  routes:
    - on: UPDATE_PROFILE
      if: "$event.payload.role == 'admin'"
      steps:
        - action: db.update
          table: users
  ```
- [ ] `if:` conditions on individual steps
- [ ] Comparison operators: `==`, `!=`, `>`, `<`, `contains`, `exists`

### Middleware
- [ ] `before:` hooks — run steps before the main route
- [ ] `after:` hooks — run steps after route completion
- [ ] `on_error:` hooks — custom error handling per route
  ```yaml
  routes:
    - on: PAYMENT_RECEIVED
      before:
        - action: auth.verify
          header: "Authorization"
      steps:
        - action: db.insert
          table: payments
      on_error:
        - action: http.post
          url: "https://alerts.slack.com/xxx"
  ```

### Authentication
- [ ] JWT validation middleware
- [ ] API key authentication
- [ ] Per-route auth requirements in manifest
  ```yaml
  nodes:
    AdminPanel:
      auth: jwt
      role: admin
  ```

---

## v1.4 — Query & Read API 📊

The missing half — reading data back, not just writing.

### Endpoints
- [ ] `GET /tables` — list all tables with row counts
- [ ] `GET /tables/:name` — query rows with filters
  ```
  GET /tables/users?email=test@dev.com&limit=10&offset=0
  ```
- [ ] `GET /tables/:name/:id` — get single row by ID
- [ ] `GET /events` — query the event audit log
  ```
  GET /events?event=SUBMIT_LEAD&since=2026-07-25T00:00:00Z&limit=50
  ```

### Event Audit Log
- [ ] Auto-log every emitted event to `_spine_events` table
- [ ] Fields: `id`, `event`, `payload`, `status`, `route`, `timestamp`, `latency_ms`
- [ ] `spine events` CLI command to query the log
- [ ] Event replay — re-emit historical events for recovery

### Manifest Queries
- [ ] `query:` blocks in manifest for pre-defined read patterns
  ```yaml
  queries:
    recent_leads:
      table: landing_analytics
      order_by: id DESC
      limit: 20
  ```

---

## v2.0 — Multi-Runtime & Plugins 🔌

Break out of single-binary mode. Support distributed architectures.

### Plugin System
- [ ] Custom action handlers via Go interfaces
  ```go
  type ActionPlugin interface {
      Name() string
      Execute(ctx context.Context, step *RouteStep, payload map[string]interface{}) error
  }
  
  engine.RegisterPlugin(&SlackNotifier{})
  engine.RegisterPlugin(&S3Uploader{})
  ```
- [ ] Load plugins from shared libraries (`.so` files)
- [ ] Plugin marketplace / registry

### Queue Integration
- [ ] `queue.publish` action — push to Redis/NATS/RabbitMQ
- [ ] `queue.subscribe` — consume from external queues as events
  ```yaml
  steps:
    - action: queue.publish
      broker: "redis://localhost:6379"
      channel: "video_processing"
      input: "$event.payload"
  ```

### Database Backends
- [ ] PostgreSQL support (swap SQLite for production)
- [ ] MySQL support
- [ ] In-memory mode (no persistence, max throughput)
- [ ] Connection pooling configuration in manifest

### Multi-File Manifests
- [ ] `include:` directive for modular manifests
  ```yaml
  spine_version: 2
  include:
    - auth.spine
    - billing.spine
    - notifications.spine
  ```

